(A7) HTTP path Atomic-construction strategy (rubber-duck issue: HTTP JSON values aren't typed proto values)
     - The webhook receives JSON: {Vin, CreatedAt, Signals: [{Name, Value, Timestamp}, ...]}.
     - Each Signal.Value is decoded by encoding/json into a Go any -- string|float64|bool|map|nil.
     - The pipeline's per-field router accepts these where a writer's bindSnapshotValue accepts the type:
         * string  -- accepted by snapshotWriter for TEXT columns and signal_log_writer kind=1.
         * float64 -- accepted by snapshotWriter for DOUBLE PRECISION columns and signal_log_writer kind=6.
         * bool    -- accepted everywhere bool is valid.
     - KNOWN GAPS (acceptable degradation -- HTTP webhook is alternative path not primary; same writers existed pre-0060 and accepted the same JSON values):
         * Setting*Unit atomics from JSON: the HYBRID drive_telemetry_writer expects fmt.Stringer for Gear -- a JSON "ShiftStateD" string passes as TEXT column verbatim. OK.
         * Compound JSON values (Location {lat,lng}, DoorState {df,dr,...}, TpmsHardWarnings {fl,fr,rl,rr}) arrive as nested maps. signal_log_writer's classify rejects map types. The router would log + fail-loud per drop-loud contract. SAME behavior pre-0060 (normalizeFleetUnits did NOT pre-flatten incoming JSON compounds for downstream signal_log writes either -- only for snapshot extractors). NOT A REGRESSION.
         * Missing per-vehicle unit context: pipeline.toSI looks up the vehicle's last seen Setting*Unit from unit_history. HTTP webhook callers historically don't emit Setting*Unit atomics; toSI is a no-op or applies the cached SI conversion. NOT A REGRESSION (same pre-0060 behavior).
     - EmittedAt: parse signal.Timestamp (per-signal) when present; fall back to payload.CreatedAt; fall back to time.Now() last. Done in TelemetryIngest before calling ProcessBatch.

