I5. internal/api/telemetry_handler_ingest.go (major rewrite)
    - Removed enums import; added errors import.
    - Added errPipelineNotWired sentinel error returned by ProcessBatch
      when h.pipeline is nil. TelemetryIngest uses errors.Is to map this
      to HTTP 503 Service Unavailable so an unwired pipeline produces a
      clear operator signal rather than a silent 200 with zero side
      effects.
    - Renamed ProcessSignals -> processSignalsLegacyDeprecated (Decision
      #6) with a // Deprecated: marker citing prompt 0090 deletion.
      Production caller count audited to ZERO post-rename — the legacy
      function is now pure dead code awaiting removal. Body retained
      minus the deleted normalize-call line.
    - Rewrote TelemetryIngest:
        * JSON-decode the FleetTelemetryBatch (unchanged).
        * Resolve VIN -> vehicleID via vehicleRepo (unchanged).
        * Build []codec.Atomic from JSON signals; EmittedAt parsed via
          parseSignalTimestamp (RFC3339Nano then RFC3339, falling back to
          batch CreatedAt then time.Now() so malformed timestamps never
          drop the batch).
        * Preserve HTTP-only side effects (raw telemetry capture to
          Mongo, per-signal Mongo log, streamingState health update for
          the /telemetry/status endpoint, MQTT republish bridge).
        * Dispatch via h.ProcessBatch — error mapping: errors.Is(err,
          errPipelineNotWired) -> 503; other errors -> 500; nil -> 200.
    - Rewrote ProcessBatch as a thin wrapper: VIN lookup -> connFSM
      heartbeat -> pipeline.ProcessAtomics. No data transformation in
      ProcessBatch — all SI conversion / routing / observer fan-out
      happens inside the pipeline (ADR-004 #2 invariant).
    - Added helpers: parseBatchTimestamp, parseSignalTimestamp,
      recordStreamingHealth, republishToMQTT.
    - DELETED normalizeFleetUnits (Decision #4) plus the three compound
      flatten helpers (flattenCompoundMapValue, flattenCompoundTimeValue,
      extractCompoundTimeField) per Decision #5 — codec.Decode already
      flattens compounds per ADR-004 #3.
    - Comment hygiene: rewrote 4 doc comments that previously named the
      deleted helper inline so the gate's grep returns 0 lines.

